
                    English Documentation for Userlist

                     This is the first release-version
                     ---------------------------------

Introduction:
=============

I  wrote  this program and the ARexx macros to replace the Userlist command
of  TransAmiga's  main  menu  as I think it is not very nice looking... :-)
TransAmiga  just  goes though the user directory and displayes the names it
finds. I soon wrote an ARexx script to replace it but now I think it is too
slow  (compared do C, Oberon, Modula 2, Pascal,...). So I started work at a
faster  solution.  I think it is now a fast working solution with a maximum
of available information. The negative thing is that the translation of the
TransAmiga  docs  to German was delayed again... (It's a lot more work than
the translation of 1.03 docs...)

Rights, responsibility:
=======================

This archive has to be distributed as is. Nobody has the right to change it
without  contacting  me!  Please  don't add any ZZZEndPads or what you call
them as they are going on the nervs.

THIS  version is freely usable. You are allowed to use the program for free
and  may  modify  the  ARexx  scripts  to your needs. I do not give away my
rights,  I  just allow every TransAmiga SysOp to use this program for free.
Future  versions (if there are any) may not be available for free. I decide
it if I finish it... I hope to give powerfull tools to TransAmiga SysOps so
they see what is possible with TransAmiga :-)

I  WARN  everybody  to  misuse  the program especially if I think about the
personal  information of the users... I hope you get what I mean as English
is  not my first language. I can not be made responsible for damage that my
be produced by the usage or misusage of the program. You use it at your own
risk!  Naturally  I  tried  to  make it as safe as possible - but nobody is
perfect!

It is possible to display the user's password so be careful and think about
the  data  you  display!  The  program can be used for online generating of
userlists  as  Userlist.trans  and UserlistGER.trans show. As this may take
some  time especially if you have lots of users and an unaccelerated Amiga,
I  think  it  is  better  to  generate  the  userlists  every  night  in  a
systemevent.  The  script  Userlistscript in BBS/BIN is to do the job. Just
call  it in your event or include it in your own scripts. Modify it to your
needs.  The  ARexx  scripts  Userlist2.trans  and Userlist2GER.trans are an
example to display the generated lists.

